## Conditional Fields via `useWatch`

Use `useWatch` (not `getValues`) to reactively show/hide fields so the UI rerenders when the watched value changes.

```tsx
const clientGroup = useWatch({ control: form.control, name: 'clientGroup' })

{clientGroup === CLIENT_GROUP.AGENT && (
  <FormField control={form.control} name="picHandleAgent" render={...} />
)}
```

When changing a watched field also clears related fields, call `setValue` inside `onValueChange`:

```tsx
onValueChange={value => {
  field.onChange(value)
  form.setValue('picHandleAgent', '')
  form.setValue('staff', null)
}}
```

---

## Cross-context Forms

In sub-components, get the parent form via `useFormContext<MyFormSchema>()` — never prop-drill the form instance.

```tsx
function SubSection() {
  const form = useFormContext<MyFormSchema>()
  return <FormField control={form.control} name="..." render={...} />
}
```

---

## Draft Persistence

For "new" records use `usePersistForm` with `sessionStorage` and a `debounceMs` to auto-save drafts. Clear on successful submit.

```tsx
const { clearStorage } = usePersistForm(form, 'my-form-draft', {
  storageType: 'sessionStorage',
  debounceMs: 1000,
  enabled: id === 'new',
})

// inside onSubmit success:
clearStorage()
```

---

## InputGroup with Inline Addon

For inline addons (icon prefix/suffix) use `InputGroupInput` instead of `Input`. Always provide `aria-label` and `type`.

```tsx
<InputGroup>
  <InputGroupAddon>
    <MailIcon aria-hidden="true" />
  </InputGroupAddon>
  <InputGroupInput
    aria-label="Contact Email"
    type="email"
    aria-invalid={!!fieldState.error}
    {...field}
  />
</InputGroup>
```

---

## Required Field Marking

Use `<span aria-required="true" className="text-destructive">*</span>` after the label text. Also set `aria-required="true"` on the input itself.

```tsx
<FormLabel>
  English Name{' '}
  <span aria-required="true" className="text-destructive">*</span>
</FormLabel>
<Input {...field} aria-required="true" />
```
